him sometimes, but,

1314
00:52:49,060 --> 00:52:51,070
he might have friends
in the inner council.

1315
00:52:51,560 --> 00:52:53,060
(all three guffawing)

1316
00:52:53,070 --> 00:52:54,570
But, I kid the pigs.

1317
00:52:54,570 --> 00:52:56,070
Let's go on inside, huh?

1318
00:52:58,070 --> 00:53:02,080
(Crow humming)

1319
00:53:02,070 --> 00:53:03,570
Big room.

1320
00:53:03,580 --> 00:53:05,580
You're late, Number Two.

1321
00:53:13,590 --> 00:53:16,090
Do you have a two-minute
song prepared?

1322
00:53:18,590 --> 00:53:20,600
Be careful.
We just vacuumed.

1323
00:53:23,600 --> 00:53:25,600
Um, can I get you
a Coke, iced tea,

1324
00:53:25,600 --> 00:53:27,100
maybe some Country Time?

1325
00:53:29,600 --> 00:53:30,610
Benedict.

1326
00:53:30,600 --> 00:53:33,600
(Tom mimicing echoing sound)

1327
00:53:35,110 --> 00:53:36,110
Good to see you.

1328
00:53:36,110 --> 00:53:38,610
(all mimicing echoing sound)

1329
00:53:39,610 --> 00:53:41,620
My colleagues and I

1330
00:53:41,610 --> 00:53:44,110
have just been
reviewing your record.

1331
00:53:44,120 --> 00:53:47,120
You were very good in
The Crucible at Circle Rep.

1332
00:53:49,120 --> 00:53:51,130
Exemplary.

1333
00:53:51,120 --> 00:53:52,120
Thank you.

1334
00:53:52,120 --> 00:53:53,620
Oh, no, no, thank you.

1335
00:53:53,630 --> 00:53:55,130
No, thank you.

1336
00:53:55,130 --> 00:53:58,130
You've more than
justified my decision to

1337
00:53:58,130 --> 00:54:01,900
name you my successor when
I moved up to the tribunal.

1338
00:54:01,900 --> 00:54:03,870
I have only
followed the policies

1339
00:54:03,870 --> 00:54:05,870
you, yourself, established.

1340
00:54:05,870 --> 00:54:08,380
You're too modest, Benedict.

1341
00:54:08,370 --> 00:54:10,370
You've improved on them.

1342
00:54:11,380 --> 00:54:12,380
But...

1343
00:54:13,380 --> 00:54:16,380
There is a matter
that concerns us.

1344
00:54:16,380 --> 00:54:17,890
Your wardrobe.

1345
00:54:19,390 --> 00:54:20,890
The Stryker affair.

1346
00:54:20,890 --> 00:54:22,390
Oh, busted!

1347
00:54:22,390 --> 00:54:24,890
I assume full
responsibility for his escape.

1348
00:54:24,890 --> 00:54:26,900
I assure you, it's
only a matter of time

1349
00:54:26,890 --> 00:54:28,890
before he's recaptured.

1350
00:54:28,890 --> 00:54:31,390
By time you mean,
later this afternoon?

1351
00:54:31,400 --> 00:54:32,900
Perhaps this evening?

1352
00:54:32,900 --> 00:54:33,900
Or tomorrow morning?

1353
00:54:33,900 --> 00:54:35,900
Hopefully, sooner than that.

1354
00:54:35,900 --> 00:54:37,410
Around sixish some time today.

1355
00:54:37,400 --> 00:54:40,900
Then you have some
idea where he is?

1356
00:54:40,910 --> 00:54:41,910
Not exactly.

1357
00:54:44,910 --> 00:54:47,420
But, we do know he's in the
company of one Dr. Cook.

1358
00:54:47,410 --> 00:54:48,910
Dr. Bettina Cook.

1359
00:54:48,910 --> 00:54:49,910
Only one?

1360
00:54:49,920 --> 00:54:51,920
He may be forcing
her to help him.

1361
00:54:51,920 --> 00:54:54,920
Or perhaps she's helping
him without being forced.

1362
00:54:54,920 --> 00:54:56,930
Yes, we haven't
overlooked that possibility.

1363
00:54:56,920 --> 00:54:58,420
Say it, don't spray it.

1364
00:54:58,420 --> 00:55:00,420
In fact, I was
about to examine

1365
00:55:00,430 --> 00:55:03,930
her citizen's profile on
her when you sent for me.

1366
00:55:03,930 --> 00:55:07,440
I intend to find out
everything about the doctor.

1367
00:55:09,440 --> 00:55:11,940
You are one sick puppy.

1368
00:55:13,940 --> 00:55:16,440
I told you there was
nothing to worry about.

1369
00:55:16,440 --> 00:55:18,950
Er, tough crowd,
yeah, tough crowd.

1370
00:55:20,450 --> 00:55:22,950
Um, I thought it
was very funny, sir,

1371
00:55:22,950 --> 00:55:23,950
If that's any help.

1372
00:55:24,450 --> 00:55:26,450
I just love his meaty neck.

1373
00:55:26,450 --> 00:55:27,460
Mmm-huh!

1374
00:55:27,450 --> 00:55:30,450
The fact that he escaped

1375
00:55:30,460 --> 00:55:31,960
will go in your record.

1376
00:55:31,960 --> 00:55:33,960
A small mark.

1377
00:55:33,960 --> 00:55:37,970
But like a single spot
on a very white surface,

1378
00:55:37,960 --> 00:55:40,460
it tends to be
extremely noticeable.

1379
00:55:40,470 --> 00:55:42,470
(mockingly) He
sounds like Sylvester.

1380
00:55:42,470 --> 00:55:46,470
The longer this Stryker
is allowed to run free,

1381
00:55:46,470 --> 00:55:49,480
the more noticeable
that spot will become.

1382
00:55:50,980 --> 00:55:52,980
Does that mean you're
gonna stop spitting on us?

1383
00:55:52,980 --> 00:55:54,480
What was that?

1384
00:55:54,480 --> 00:55:57,490
- Oh, nothing.
- I understand.

1385
00:55:58,980 --> 00:56:00,480
I knew you would.

1386
00:56:00,490 --> 00:56:02,490
Eh, stick it, Baldie.

1387
00:56:02,490 --> 00:56:03,990
- What was that?
- Uh, nothing, sir.

1388
00:56:03,990 --> 00:56:05,490
I said I'd get 'em all.

1389
00:56:07,490 --> 00:56:08,990
Go away.

1390
00:56:12,000 --> 00:56:13,500
Oh, and, see my tailor.

1391
00:56:13,500 --> 00:56:16,000
He'll fix you up with
some nice, new clothes.

1392
00:56:17,500 --> 00:56:20,000
(all three exclaiming)

1393
00:56:20,010 --> 00:56:22,010
Same trees. Flowers.

1394
00:56:22,010 --> 00:56:23,510
It's like a dream.

1395
00:56:23,510 --> 00:56:25,010
A made-for-TV dream.

1396
00:56:25,010 --> 00:56:26,510
Perhaps, but for many years,

1397
00:56:26,510 --> 00:56:28,020
our scientists have
discussed the possibility

1398
00:56:28,010 --> 00:56:29,010
of a Terra twin.

1399
00:56:29,010 --> 00:56:31,010
As your scientists
must also have done.

1400
00:56:31,520 --> 00:56:32,520
That is, two planets,

1401
00:56:32,520 --> 00:56:34,520
flung out from the
sun at the same time.

1402
00:56:34,520 --> 00:56:36,520
Both of equal size and gravity,

1403
00:56:36,520 --> 00:56:38,530
and orbiting exactly opposite,

1404
00:56:38,520 --> 00:56:41,020
so that neither
ever sees the other.

1405
00:56:41,030 --> 00:56:43,030
Cooling simultaneously.

1406
00:56:43,030 --> 00:56:44,530
Oceans forming together.

1407
00:56:45,030 --> 00:56:48,040
And the first germs of life
appearing there, as here.

1408
00:56:48,030 --> 00:56:51,030
It's two, two,
two worlds in one.

1409
00:56:51,040 --> 00:56:54,040
Nothing exists by
chance in life, Neil.

1410
00:56:54,040 --> 00:56:56,040
Effect and cause,
cause and effect.

1411
00:56:56,040 --> 00:56:57,050
Precisely.

1412
00:56:57,040 --> 00:56:58,040
I think he's got it!

1413
00:56:58,040 --> 00:56:59,040
As life developed
here on Terra,

1414
00:56:59,550 --> 00:57:01,550
its counterpart
developed on its twin.

1415
00:57:01,550 --> 00:57:03,050
For every mountain
and valley here,

1416
00:57:03,050 --> 00:57:04,550
its counterpart developed there.

1417
00:57:05,050 --> 00:57:07,060
And so on through
the many long ages.

1418
00:57:07,050 --> 00:57:08,550
And so on, and
so on, and so on.

1419
00:57:08,550 --> 00:57:11,050
What did you call
your planet again?

1420
00:57:11,060 --> 00:57:13,060
Earth.

1421
00:57:13,060 --> 00:57:14,560
Dirt? Oh, Earth.

1422
00:57:14,560 --> 00:57:17,570
Has a very nice sound.

1423
00:57:17,560 --> 00:57:20,560
But I kid the other planets.

1424
00:57:20,570 --> 00:57:22,070
Kill him.

1425
00:57:23,570 --> 00:57:25,570
Now everybody
bring their suit?

1426
00:57:25,570 --> 00:57:28,580
We could skinny-dip. (chuckles)

1427
00:57:28,570 --> 00:57:31,570
Oh, this must be Terra's
Funniest Home Videos.

1428
00:57:33,580 --> 00:57:34,580
Oh, it's Out of This World

1429
00:57:34,580 --> 00:57:37,590
with Donna Pescow
and Doug McClure.

1430
00:57:37,580 --> 00:57:39,080
And, tonight on Star Search,

1431
00:57:39,080 --> 00:57:41,580
in the lab technician category.

1432
00:57:44,090 --> 00:57:47,100
Hey, it's the Miss
Alternate Universe pageant!

1433
00:57:52,600 --> 00:57:55,100
Uh, The Rick Dees
Show renewed again.

1434
00:57:55,100 --> 00:57:56,100
I don't get it.

1435
00:57:56,100 --> 00:57:58,610
Well, back where we started.

1436
00:57:58,600 --> 00:58:00,600
She has to turn up some place.

1437
00:58:00,610 --> 00:58:03,110
All of her friends are under
protective surveillance.

1438
00:58:03,110 --> 00:58:07,120
You mean the
friends we know about.

1439
00:58:07,110 --> 00:58:08,610
What about the ones we don't?

1440
00:58:08,610 --> 00:58:11,110
Like her poker buddies.

1441
00:58:11,120 --> 00:58:13,120
Oh, it's a possibility, Henry.

1442
00:58:14,120 --> 00:58:16,120
One we can't overlook.

1443
00:58:17,620 --> 00:58:20,120
I want that Rockford
matter taken care of.

1444
00:58:20,130 --> 00:58:22,630
Permanently.

1445
00:58:22,630 --> 00:58:24,130
So, you, uh,
heard about me?

1446
00:58:24,130 --> 00:58:26,130
We heard rumors that an
unidentified spacecraft

1447
00:58:26,630 --> 00:58:27,640
had been brought down,

1448
00:58:27,630 --> 00:58:29,630
and an astronaut taken
to the medical center.

1449
00:58:29,640 --> 00:58:31,640
Well, there were two
others on board with me.

1450
00:58:31,640 --> 00:58:33,640
We heard they were dead.

1451
00:58:33,640 --> 00:58:36,140
- And buried.
- In that order.

1452
00:58:36,140 --> 00:58:37,150
Where?

1453
00:58:37,140 --> 00:58:39,140
I don't know.

1454
00:58:40,650 --> 00:58:42,150
No services or prayers?

1455
00:58:42,150 --> 00:58:43,650
Or snacks?

1456
00:58:43,650 --> 00:58:46,150
Some of our older
people still pray.

1457
00:58:46,150 --> 00:58:48,160
But very softly, I'm afraid.

1458
00:58:48,150 --> 00:58:49,650
Kinda like nuns.

1459
00:58:49,660 --> 00:58:52,160
Religion has been outlawed
by the Perfect Order.

1460
00:58:52,160 --> 00:58:54,660
How did this Perfect
Order come about?

1461
00:58:54,660 --> 00:58:56,660
Oh, sarcasm.

1462
00:58:58,660 --> 00:59:01,660
Well, it seems we closed
our eyes for a little while,

1463
00:59:01,670 --> 00:59:03,170
and when we opened them again,

1464
00:59:03,170 --> 00:59:05,170
- Reagan was in office.
- It was here.

1465
00:59:05,170 --> 00:59:06,670
Can't you do
something about it?

1466
00:59:06,670 --> 00:59:08,180
What would you suggest?

1467
00:59:08,170 --> 00:59:10,670
Well, if enough
people oppose something!

1468
00:59:10,680 --> 00:59:12,180
How can puppets and--

1469
00:59:12,180 --> 00:59:13,680
- I resent that.
- Yeah, me too.

1470
00:59:14,180 --> 00:59:15,680
Men like yourself!

1471
00:59:15,680 --> 00:59:17,690
Toothless warriors.

1472
00:59:17,680 --> 00:59:18,680
Get dentures!

1473
00:59:18,680 --> 00:59:20,680
There's been a few
young men brave enough

1474
00:59:20,690 --> 00:59:21,690
to make their voices heard.

1475
00:59:21,690 --> 00:59:24,190
Young men who
disappear in the night.

1476
00:59:24,190 --> 00:59:27,700
All record of their births
and accomplishments destroyed.

1477
00:59:27,690 --> 00:59:30,690
Their families forbidden to
mention their names in public.

1478
00:59:30,700 --> 00:59:32,200
Like my uncle, oh,
oh, I did it again.

1479
00:59:32,200 --> 00:59:34,200
It's one thing
to have died, Neil.

1480
00:59:34,200 --> 00:59:37,210
Another never to have existed.

1481
00:59:37,200 --> 00:59:40,200
And then there's, uh, Ward E.

1482
00:59:40,210 --> 00:59:41,710
The Time Tunnel.

1483
00:59:41,710 --> 00:59:42,710
In color.

1484
00:59:42,710 --> 00:59:44,710
Oh, Ward E!

1485
00:59:52,720 --> 00:59:55,220
So, I hear they're filming
Get Smart on this set.

1486
01:00:01,730 --> 01:00:02,730
Hi.

1487
01:00:02,730 --> 01:00:03,730
Now then, you were
looking for something

1488
01:00:03,730 --> 01:00:05,230
in a deck shoe, I believe.

1489
01:00:10,240 --> 01:00:12,740
Ah, I like what you've
done with the place.

1490
01:00:12,740 --> 01:00:14,740
- Dr. Revere?
- I had Jell-O today.

1491
01:00:14,740 --> 01:00:16,240
Can you hear me?

1492
01:00:20,250 --> 01:00:23,250
You realize, of course, that
this is for your own good?

1493
01:00:23,250 --> 01:00:26,250
Lobotomy means never
having to say you're sorry.

1494
01:00:26,250 --> 01:00:27,260
Or anything else.

1495
01:00:27,750 --> 01:00:29,250
You were tired, Doctor.

1496
01:00:29,250 --> 01:00:30,750
You needed rest.

1497
01:00:30,760 --> 01:00:34,260
And that chair is
very restful, isn't it?

1498
01:00:34,260 --> 01:00:36,760
Now, Doctor, you can help me.

1499
01:00:39,770 --> 01:00:42,770
You do wanna help me,
don't you, Doctor?

1500
01:00:42,770 --> 01:00:43,770
Oh, I do.

1501
01:00:43,770 --> 01:00:45,770
That would please me to no end.

1502
01:00:45,770 --> 01:00:49,280
All you'll have to do is
tell me about Bettina Cook.

1503
01:00:49,780 --> 01:00:52,280
You were her professor
at the university.

1504
01:00:52,280 --> 01:00:55,780
She took advanced training
from you at the hospital.

1505
01:00:55,780 --> 01:00:58,790
We know that she
confided in you.

1506
01:00:58,780 --> 01:01:03,280
You know, of course, her
loyalty to the Perfect Order.

1507
01:01:03,290 --> 01:01:05,290
But, would Bettina
have any friends

1508
01:01:05,290 --> 01:01:07,300
that we don't know about?

1509
01:01:07,290 --> 01:01:10,290
I mean, if she thought that
we were looking for her,

1510
01:01:10,300 --> 01:01:13,300
is there some place
she could hide?

1511
01:01:13,300 --> 01:01:16,300
Well, she's got a tree fort.

1512
01:01:16,300 --> 01:01:17,810
Come on, Doctor.

1513
01:01:17,800 --> 01:01:20,300
You do understand me.

1514
01:01:20,310 --> 01:01:22,310
You're protecting her.

1515
01:01:22,310 --> 01:01:25,310
Why? Hmm?

1516
01:01:25,310 --> 01:01:27,820
Where is she?

1517
01:01:27,810 --> 01:01:29,310
Where is Betinna Cook?

1518
01:01:29,820 --> 01:01:32,320
Betinna Cook.

1519
01:01:32,320 --> 01:01:34,320
Betinna Cook, Doctor.

1520
01:01:34,320 --> 01:01:35,320
Betinna Cook.

1521
01:01:35,320 --> 01:01:37,830
I heard ya the first time!

1522
01:01:41,830 --> 01:01:42,830
Oh, he's been like this

1523
01:01:42,830 --> 01:01:45,330
ever since he
started watching MTV.

1524
01:01:46,830 --> 01:01:47,840
That far?

1525
01:01:47,830 --> 01:01:50,330
I was told by your assistant

1526
01:01:50,340 --> 01:01:52,240
he was no further use to us.

1527
01:01:53,640 --> 01:01:56,140
What are we going
to do with you?

1528
01:01:56,140 --> 01:01:58,150
Uh, get me drunk?

1529
01:01:59,650 --> 01:02:01,650
Is it possible for me
to get back to Earth?

1530
01:02:02,150 --> 01:02:03,650
Anything's possible.

1531
01:02:03,650 --> 01:02:06,650
The fact that you got here in
the first place proves that.

1532
01:02:06,650 --> 01:02:10,160
Besides, Terra has a very
active space program.

1533
01:02:10,160 --> 01:02:13,160
Our crafts have great
range and capabilities.

1534
01:02:13,160 --> 01:02:15,660
- Are they ground controlled?
- To Major Tom?

1535
01:02:15,660 --> 01:02:17,170
Only during blast-off.

1536
01:02:17,160 --> 01:02:21,160
After that, the astronaut has
complete control of his ship.

1537
01:02:21,170 --> 01:02:23,170
Then all I have to
do is get aboard one.

1538
01:02:23,170 --> 01:02:26,670
Oh, (chuckles) you
make it sound like, uh,

1539
01:02:26,670 --> 01:02:28,180
catching a train.

1540
01:02:28,170 --> 01:02:30,170
There has to be a way, Dylan.

1541
01:02:30,680 --> 01:02:31,680
Thomas.

1542
01:02:31,680 --> 01:02:33,680
Hmm, maybe there is.

1543
01:02:33,680 --> 01:02:35,680
With my help.

1544
01:02:35,680 --> 01:02:38,190
Oh, I can't let you risk it.

1545
01:02:38,180 --> 01:02:39,680
But you can't
deprive an old man

1546
01:02:39,690 --> 01:02:43,690
of the one pleasure he
enjoys most in life.

1547
01:02:43,690 --> 01:02:45,190
Outwitting the Perfect Order.

1548
01:02:45,190 --> 01:02:46,690
Oh, I'm glad you said that.

1549
01:02:46,690 --> 01:02:48,200
Now, if you
could change places

1550
01:02:48,190 --> 01:02:49,690
with one of our astronauts.

1551
01:02:49,700 --> 01:02:52,200
Wouldn't it have to be
right before the launch?

1552
01:02:52,200 --> 01:02:54,700
That's when he has the
most people around him.

1553
01:02:54,700 --> 01:02:56,200
What about when
he's suiting up?

1554
01:02:56,200 --> 01:02:57,710
There's a guard
outside his room,

1555
01:02:57,700 --> 01:02:59,200
and a technician helping him.

1556
01:02:59,200 --> 01:03:01,700
All right.
That narrows it to two.

1557
01:03:01,710 --> 01:03:03,210
You'd only have about 30
minutes to make the switch.

1558
01:03:03,210 --> 01:03:04,210
That's all I need.

1559
01:03:04,210 --> 01:03:06,210
But even if you
got aboard, Neil,

1560
01:03:06,210 --> 01:03:08,220
could you handle the craft?

1561
01:03:08,210 --> 01:03:10,210
I'd sure give it a try.

1562
01:03:10,220 --> 01:03:11,720
You're cute.

1563
01:03:11,720 --> 01:03:14,720
It would help if I could
study some operations manuals.

1564
01:03:14,720 --> 01:03:17,230
I have all of them.

1565
01:03:17,220 --> 01:03:18,720
(moaning, glass breaking)

1566
01:03:18,720 --> 01:03:20,720
In my sternum!

1567
01:03:20,730 --> 01:03:22,730
The little black box.

1568
01:03:22,730 --> 01:03:24,730
Small table. Living room.

1569
01:03:24,730 --> 01:03:26,730
A bureau? Hutch?

1570
01:03:27,730 --> 01:03:30,730
Neil, Neil?

1571
01:03:30,740 --> 01:03:33,240
The television.

1572
01:03:33,240 --> 01:03:36,240
Oh, yeah, Pat Sajak
