01:27:09,850 --> 01:27:11,850
I took a slug in the arm.

2093
01:27:13,360 --> 01:27:14,560
I want him.

2094
01:27:16,060 --> 01:27:18,060
Boy, this is the biggest
basement I've ever seen.

2095
01:27:18,060 --> 01:27:20,570
What, are they in
Aaron Spelling's house?

2096
01:27:20,560 --> 01:27:22,060
(sirens in distance)

2097
01:27:22,070 --> 01:27:23,070
Goes on forever.

2098
01:27:23,070 --> 01:27:26,570
(sirens wailing)

2099
01:27:28,070 --> 01:27:29,580
The Rat Patrol.

2100
01:27:29,570 --> 01:27:31,070
In color.

2101
01:27:31,070 --> 01:27:35,070
(suspenseful music)

2102
01:27:35,080 --> 01:27:39,090
(Tom mocking music)

2103
01:27:39,080 --> 01:27:39,580
Oh, man.

2104
01:27:39,580 --> 01:27:41,080
Clowns to left of me,

2105
01:27:41,080 --> 01:27:42,080
jokers to my right.

2106
01:27:42,090 --> 01:27:45,090
Here I am, stuck in
a made-for-TV-movie,

2107
01:27:45,090 --> 01:27:46,090
with you.

2108
01:27:48,590 --> 01:27:53,100
(Tom mocking music)

2109
01:27:58,100 --> 01:27:59,610
All right, friend.

2110
01:27:59,600 --> 01:28:01,600
Prepare to meet Kali.

2111
01:28:01,610 --> 01:28:04,110
In hell. (chuckles)

2112
01:28:06,610 --> 01:28:07,610
What's he gonna do?

2113
01:28:07,610 --> 01:28:10,120
I mean, there's
really no way out.

2114
01:28:10,110 --> 01:28:12,110
No, this is the end for him.

2115
01:28:12,120 --> 01:28:13,120
Yeah, pretty much just,

2116
01:28:13,120 --> 01:28:14,620
they take him and he surrenders.

2117
01:28:14,620 --> 01:28:18,120
(humming)

2118
01:28:18,120 --> 01:28:19,630
Lotta sexual tension, though.

2119
01:28:19,620 --> 01:28:21,620
Yeah, I'll give you that.

2120
01:28:21,630 --> 01:28:24,130
(humming)

2121
01:28:24,130 --> 01:28:27,130
It looks like Acapulco
over here by the cliff.

2122
01:28:27,130 --> 01:28:29,640
(humming)

2123
01:28:29,630 --> 01:28:30,630
Oh!

2124
01:28:30,630 --> 01:28:33,630
Next week on MacGyver.

2125
01:28:33,640 --> 01:28:35,140
Krakatoa, east of Java.

2126
01:28:35,140 --> 01:28:37,140
Check it out.

2127
01:28:37,140 --> 01:28:38,640
Out of focus.

2128
01:28:38,640 --> 01:28:41,650
(alarms blaring)

2129
01:28:41,650 --> 01:28:43,150
Oh, hi, Rick.

2130
01:28:43,150 --> 01:28:46,150
Looks like he just heard
from Dean Witter. (chuckles)

2131
01:28:50,150 --> 01:28:51,650
Wardrobe!

2132
01:28:51,660 --> 01:28:53,160
Nothin' up my sleeve.

2133
01:28:54,160 --> 01:28:55,160
Again?

2134
01:29:00,660 --> 01:29:02,660
Get out of my way.

2135
01:29:04,170 --> 01:29:05,670
The closer he gets.

2136
01:29:05,670 --> 01:29:07,670
The better she looks.

2137
01:29:07,670 --> 01:29:09,180
Well, maybe not.

2138
01:29:09,170 --> 01:29:12,170
(emulating Bettina)
Are you still mad?

2139
01:29:16,180 --> 01:29:19,190
You did the right
thing, Bettina.

2140
01:29:19,180 --> 01:29:21,180
Thanks to the Perfect Order,

2141
01:29:21,180 --> 01:29:23,180
we have one great
family here on Terra.

2142
01:29:23,190 --> 01:29:25,190
A dysfunctional family, but.

2143
01:29:25,190 --> 01:29:27,690
Destined to
protect each other.

2144
01:29:27,690 --> 01:29:30,700
Destined to help each other.

2145
01:29:30,690 --> 01:29:33,690
Destined to look
after each other.

2146
01:29:33,700 --> 01:29:37,200
Destined to be trapped
in made-for-TV movies.

2147
01:29:37,200 --> 01:29:40,710
My brother lives in Florida.

2148
01:29:40,700 --> 01:29:42,200
Gum?

2149
01:29:42,210 --> 01:29:44,710
He couldn't have
survived the explosion.

2150
01:29:44,710 --> 01:29:46,710
I want proof of this.

2151
01:29:46,710 --> 01:29:47,710
I want proof.

2152
01:29:47,710 --> 01:29:49,220
Proof?

2153
01:29:49,210 --> 01:29:51,710
His charred
bones, if necessary.

2154
01:29:51,720 --> 01:29:53,220
Mmm, charred bones, mmm.

2155
01:29:53,220 --> 01:29:55,220
One of the men found this.

2156
01:29:55,220 --> 01:29:57,720
Stryker must've lost it on his
way to the chemical building.

2157
01:30:01,730 --> 01:30:04,230
Didn't think it'd fit
in my pants, did ya?

2158
01:30:06,730 --> 01:30:08,230
Can't see.

2159
01:30:14,240 --> 01:30:15,240
Oh, he dropped the thing

2160
01:30:15,240 --> 01:30:17,240
that's gonna drive
the whole series.

2161
01:30:22,250 --> 01:30:25,250
Drop in any mailbox,
postage guaranteed.

2162
01:30:26,250 --> 01:30:27,750
(mimicking Bettina) I
had forgotten his name

2163
01:30:28,250 --> 01:30:29,760
after the lobotomy.

2164
01:30:31,760 --> 01:30:34,260
Kinda ran her pantyhose
there, didn't she?

2165
01:30:34,260 --> 01:30:37,260
Yeah, it's been a
crappy day for her.

2166
01:30:37,260 --> 01:30:39,270
Lemme tell ya.

2167
01:30:39,260 --> 01:30:41,260
Calgon, take her away.

2168
01:30:44,770 --> 01:30:47,270
(Joel sputtering)

2169
01:30:47,270 --> 01:30:48,270
Water.

2170
01:30:48,270 --> 01:30:50,280
The source of all bad acting.

2171
01:30:50,270 --> 01:30:51,770
And how.

2172
01:30:55,280 --> 01:30:58,280
And so, standing erect,
he emerged from the slime.

2173
01:31:00,280 --> 01:31:03,780
(groaning) This looks
like a good place.

2174
01:31:05,790 --> 01:31:07,790
He's his own From
Here to Eternity.

2175
01:31:08,290 --> 01:31:10,300
Oh, now, what is it?

2176
01:31:17,300 --> 01:31:19,310
What happened?

2177
01:31:19,300 --> 01:31:21,300
(coughing) From other planet.

2178
01:31:21,300 --> 01:31:22,800
Thing crashed.

2179
01:31:22,810 --> 01:31:23,810
Had girlfriend.

2180
01:31:23,810 --> 01:31:25,310
Blew stuff up.

2181
01:31:25,310 --> 01:31:26,310
Capsized.

2182
01:31:26,310 --> 01:31:28,810
I had to swim to shore.

2183
01:31:29,310 --> 01:31:30,810
Ah, made for TV, huh?

2184
01:31:30,810 --> 01:31:32,310
Joe, get me my coat.

2185
01:31:32,320 --> 01:31:34,320
But not the good one!

2186
01:31:38,320 --> 01:31:39,830
We've been, uh,

2187
01:31:39,820 --> 01:31:42,320
we've been campin'
here a couple days.

2188
01:31:42,330 --> 01:31:45,330
We're gettin' ready to
leave in a little while.

2189
01:31:45,330 --> 01:31:46,830
Which way you goin'?

2190
01:31:49,330 --> 01:31:51,330
Uh, up the coast.

2191
01:31:51,330 --> 01:31:52,330
So are we.

2192
01:31:52,340 --> 01:31:53,840
Yeah, toward Stephen
Cannell's house.

2193
01:31:53,840 --> 01:31:55,840
You're welcome to ride
with us if you want.

2194
01:31:55,840 --> 01:31:57,340
But sit on a towel.

2195
01:31:57,340 --> 01:31:59,350
Thanks.

2196
01:32:01,340 --> 01:32:03,340
Here, friend.

2197
01:32:03,350 --> 01:32:05,350
Nice.

2198
01:32:07,850 --> 01:32:09,860
My name's Mitchell.

2199
01:32:09,850 --> 01:32:10,850
Cameron.

2200
01:32:10,850 --> 01:32:11,850
James Mitchell.

2201
01:32:11,860 --> 01:32:12,860
Yeah, right.

2202
01:32:12,860 --> 01:32:14,360
And my name's Peter Rabbit.

2203
01:32:14,360 --> 01:32:15,860
Tom Nelson.

2204
01:32:16,860 --> 01:32:17,860
Mike Nelson.

2205
01:32:17,860 --> 01:32:20,370
Come along.

2206
01:32:20,360 --> 01:32:22,860
Does that guy
realize he's gonna get

2207
01:32:22,870 --> 01:32:26,870
a lobotomy just for
fraternizing with that guy?

2208
01:32:26,870 --> 01:32:29,380
Oh, what the heck.

2209
01:32:30,370 --> 01:32:32,370
So long, Chinese lanterns.

2210
01:32:35,380 --> 01:32:38,380
Is it possible for me
to get back to Earth?

2211
01:32:38,380 --> 01:32:40,390
Anything's possible.

2212
01:32:40,380 --> 01:32:44,880
The fact that you got here in
the first place proves that.

2213
01:32:44,890 --> 01:32:46,890
What?

2214
01:32:46,890 --> 01:32:50,400
That doesn't sound the same.

2215
01:32:50,390 --> 01:32:53,390
It's our old friend Karl
Demer again, isn't it?

2216
01:32:53,400 --> 01:32:55,400
It's the big
pretzel in space.

2217
01:32:55,400 --> 01:32:58,900
Hey, they're getting
better with these holy-grams.

2218
01:32:58,900 --> 01:33:01,910
They changed that
one back and forth.

2219
01:33:01,910 --> 01:33:04,410
Music by Kraftwerk.

2220
01:33:04,410 --> 01:33:07,410
It sounds more like
Super Mario music to me.

2221
01:33:07,410 --> 01:33:08,910
You know,

2222
01:33:08,910 --> 01:33:10,420
this movie was originally
titled The Stranger,

2223
01:33:10,410 --> 01:33:12,910
but, you know, I didn't see
anybody dying on the beach.

2224
01:33:12,920 --> 01:33:14,920
It doesn't look anything
like Camus to me.

2225
01:33:15,420 --> 01:33:16,920
I don't understand.

2226
01:33:18,420 --> 01:33:20,930
Fun, fun, fun in the autobahn.

2227
01:33:20,920 --> 01:33:24,920
Autobahn, autobahn,
pa-tom-pom-pom.

2228
01:33:24,930 --> 01:33:27,930
Can we get outta
here now, please?

2229
01:33:29,930 --> 01:33:32,930
Another day,
another food tablet.

2230
01:33:32,940 --> 01:33:37,940
(metal sliding and clanging)

2231
01:33:41,910 --> 01:33:44,380
Looking forward to
lunch at The Polo.

2232
01:33:44,380 --> 01:33:45,890
Yours truly, Tommy Servo,

2233
01:33:45,880 --> 01:33:47,880
executive in charge
of production,

2234
01:33:47,880 --> 01:33:49,880
Satellite of Love Studios,
et cetera, et cetera.

2235
01:33:49,890 --> 01:33:51,390
Hey, read that
back to me, honey,

2236
01:33:51,390 --> 01:33:52,890
will ya, Magic Voice, baby?

2237
01:33:52,890 --> 01:33:54,390
Dear Mr. Ovitz.

2238
01:33:54,390 --> 01:33:56,400
You just don't know how to
take no for an answer, do you?

2239
01:33:56,390 --> 01:33:57,890
Uh, Mr. Servo.

2240
01:33:57,890 --> 01:34:00,390
There's a Joel Robinson
and a Crow here to see you.

2241
01:34:00,400 --> 01:34:01,400
Oh, send 'em in.

2242
01:34:01,400 --> 01:34:03,400
We'll go over that letter lady.

2243
01:34:03,400 --> 01:34:04,900
Okay, whadda you two
pixies got for me?

2244
01:34:04,900 --> 01:34:06,910
It better be hot,
better be good.

2245
01:34:06,900 --> 01:34:07,900
Uh, did you see
the movie, sir?

2246
01:34:07,900 --> 01:34:09,900
Did you see Stranded in Space?

2247
01:34:09,910 --> 01:34:10,910
Yeah.

2248
01:34:10,910 --> 01:34:11,410
Yeah, what'd you think?

2249
01:34:11,410 --> 01:34:12,410
Dynamite, huh?

2250
01:34:12,910 --> 01:34:13,910
And what a series it'll make.

2251
01:34:13,910 --> 01:34:14,910
A series?

2252
01:34:14,910 --> 01:34:16,420
Oh, come on.

2253
01:34:16,410 --> 01:34:17,410
Look, kid, I was thinkin'
it was an okay pilot,

2254
01:34:17,410 --> 01:34:18,910
but I just don't see
it as a series, please.

2255
01:34:18,920 --> 01:34:20,420
Are you kidding?

2256
01:34:20,420 --> 01:34:21,420
It's got all the ingredients!

2257
01:34:21,420 --> 01:34:23,420
It's The Fugitive
meets Logan's Run

2258
01:34:23,420 --> 01:34:25,420
with Please Don't Eat
the Daisies sprinkled in.

2259
01:34:25,420 --> 01:34:25,930
It can't miss!

2260
01:34:25,920 --> 01:34:27,420
Oh, come on.

2261
01:34:27,420 --> 01:34:29,420
Look, look, if Stranded in Space
becomes a series,

2262
01:34:29,430 --> 01:34:30,430
that lead has got to go.

2263
01:34:30,430 --> 01:34:32,430
I was thinkin' of
maybe David Janssen.

2264
01:34:32,430 --> 01:34:33,430
Yeah.

2265
01:34:33,430 --> 01:34:35,430
But, uh, David Janssen's dead.

2266
01:34:35,430 --> 01:34:36,940
Oh, and that actor
there was alive?

2267
01:34:36,930 --> 01:34:38,430
Gimme a break, come on.

2268
01:34:38,440 --> 01:34:39,440
'Scuse me, Mr. Servo.

2269
01:34:39,440 --> 01:34:40,940
the Maitre D' at
Spago just called,

2270
01:34:40,940 --> 01:34:42,940
and I'm sorry, there are no
tables available tonight.

2271
01:34:42,940 --> 01:34:44,440
Oh, heck.

2272
01:34:44,440 --> 01:34:45,950
I guess I'll just have to
use the drive-through, then.

2273
01:34:45,940 --> 01:34:46,940
Okay.

2274
01:34:46,940 --> 01:34:47,940
David Geffen on line three.

2275
01:34:47,940 --> 01:34:48,940
Geffen?

2276
01:34:48,950 --> 01:34:50,450
Oh, I'm gonna take that call.

2277
01:34:50,450 --> 01:34:51,450
Hey, look, Joel, press that
button for me, will ya?

2278
01:34:51,450 --> 01:34:52,950
My arms are inoperative, babe.

2279
01:34:52,950 --> 01:34:53,950
Thank you.

2280
01:34:53,950 --> 01:34:54,950
Say, Geffen.

2281
01:34:54,950 --> 01:34:56,960
Hey, look, I'm very upset.

2282
01:34:56,950 --> 01:34:58,450
Listen, I'm very upset.

2283
01:34:58,460 --> 01:35:00,460
You assure me that Kevin
Costner and Julia Roberts

2284
01:35:00,460 --> 01:35:01,460
are all set to sign.

2285
01:35:01,460 --> 01:35:02,460
Now you tell me they
been replaced by

2286
01:35:02,960 --> 01:35:03,960
Bill Bixby and Joanne Whalley?

2287
01:35:03,960 --> 01:35:06,470
I'm gonna plotz right
here, you listen to me?

2288
01:35:06,460 --> 01:35:07,960
I consider it as a
personal betrayal.

2289
01:35:07,960 --> 01:35:08,960
I'm gonna bury you man.

2290
01:35:08,970 --> 01:35:10,470
Do you hear me?
Bury you.

2291
01:35:10,470 --> 01:35:11,470
Get outta my face.

2292
01:35:11,470 --> 01:35:13,470
Um, you know, Mr. Servo,

2293
01:35:13,470 --> 01:35:15,470
I think we should
read this letter.

2294
01:35:15,470 --> 01:35:16,480
Yeah, why not?
Sure.

2295
01:35:16,970 --> 01:35:17,970
Dear MST3K.

2296
01:35:17,970 --> 01:35:20,470
My husband is a big
fan of this program.

2297
01:35:20,480 --> 01:35:21,480
He is 52 years old,

2298
01:35:21,480 --> 01:35:22,980
and he's an aircraft mechanic.

2299
01:35:22,980 --> 01:35:24,480
He never misses it.

2300
01:35:24,480 --> 01:35:25,480
His name is Bob.

2301
01:35:25,480 --> 01:35:27,490
It's from Dee Moore.

2302
01:35:27,480 --> 01:35:28,980
Oh, that's beautiful.

2303
01:35:28,990 --> 01:35:30,490
I love it.

2304
01:35:30,490 --> 01:35:31,490
I can see Gil Gerard as
Bob, the aircraft mechanic.

2305
01:35:31,490 --> 01:35:34,490
Lindsay Wagner as Dee,
his long-suffering wife.

2306
01:35:34,490 --> 01:35:35,490
Oh, boy, it's beautiful.

2307
01:35:35,490 --> 01:35:36,000
It's got legs, it's got heat.

2308
01:35:36,490 --> 01:35:37,490
It's got everything.

2309
01:35:37,490 --> 01:35:38,490
Sign 'em up!

2310
01:35:38,500 --> 01:35:41,500
What did you think, sirs?

2311
01:35:41,500 --> 01:35:44,000
Ah, show business
and mad science.

2312
01:35:44,000 --> 01:35:47,510
Two very fickle, very
unstable professions.

2313
01:35:47,500 --> 01:35:51,500
You know, Frank, I may be forced
out of my position one day,

2314
01:35:51,510 --> 01:35:54,510
and a replacement
will have to be found.

2315
01:35:54,510 --> 01:35:55,510
Really?

2316
01:35:55,510 --> 01:35:56,020
Yes.

2317
01:35:56,510 --> 01:35:57,010
An assistant, perhaps.

2318
01:35:57,510 --> 01:35:59,010
Someone next in line.

2319
01:35:59,020 --> 01:36:00,520
Well, what?

2320
01:36:00,520 --> 01:36:02,520
We put an ad in the paper,
or something like that?

2321
01:36:02,520 --> 01:36:04,520
Frank, you just don't get it.

2322
01:36:04,520 --> 01:36:06,030
In all likelihood,

2323
01:36:06,020 --> 01:36:07,020
it would be someone from right
here at Gizmonic Institute.

2324
01:36:07,020 --> 01:36:11,020
Someone who's worked
very closely with me.

2325
01:36:11,030 --> 01:36:14,030
(scoffing) And then I
have to train 'im in, right?

2326
01:36:14,030 --> 01:36:16,040
Oh, Frank, Frank.

2327
01:36:16,030 --> 01:36:19,030
I offer you the world and all
you see is middle management.

2328
01:36:19,040 --> 01:36:20,540
Push the button.

2329
01:36:20,540 --> 01:36:23,040
Hey, is this suit
coming outta my salary?

2330
01:36:23,540 --> 01:36:25,040
(sighing)

2331
01:36:26,840 --> 01:36:31,840
("Mighty Science Theater")

